# C# conventions (analyzers are errors)

Build already fails on CA/IDE issues (`TreatWarningsAsErrors`, `AnalysisMode=All`). Do not silence analyzers or widen suppressions to get green.

Prefer real fixes: null-flow narrowing, primary constructors, collection expressions, exhaustive switches, one type per file (SA1402). Suppressions only when a third-party API forces a false positive, kept minimal and justified next to the suppression.
